"""
FastAPI backend for the recorder. Same 3 operations as before, now as a
proper JSON API consumed by the Next.js frontend (frontend/) or anything
else you want to point at it (curl, Postman, another UI) - plus auth
(backend/auth_routes.py), admin (backend/admin_routes.py) and profile
(backend/profile_routes.py) routers mounted below. Every /api/* route in
this file now requires a logged-in user (Depends(get_current_user)); admin
endpoints live in their own router.

Logging: see logging.ini / logging_setup.py - everything from INFO up goes
to logs/app.log, ERROR and up (including full tracebacks - see the global
exception handler below and the per-stage try/excepts in stop_and_save)
also goes to logs/error.log, and both mirror to the console. A bare 500
with no detail (like "Save & Generate failed: 500 Server Error") should
always have a matching traceback in logs/error.log after this - if it
doesn't, logging.ini itself failed to load (logging_setup falls back to a
bare console-only config and logs a warning about that specifically).

Run with:
    uvicorn backend.api:app --reload --port 8000 --reload-dir backend --reload-dir auth \
        --reload-dir database --reload-dir recorder --reload-dir generator --reload-dir runner \
        --reload-dir agent

(the --reload-dir flags keep the reloader from watching output/, recordings/,
transactions/ and logs/ - all written to continuously during a recording or
test run - which would otherwise restart the dev server mid-execution; see
the reload_dirs= passed to uvicorn.run() below for the `python backend/api.py`
equivalent.)
"""
